  "worked_solution": "Since we want to find the projection onto the $xy$-plane, we need to eliminate the variable $z.$ First, we solve the equation of the plane for $z,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n2z-x-10=0\\,⟹\\,z=\\frac{x}{2}+5\n$$\n\nSubstituting the expression for $z$ into the equation of the elliptic cone, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}+(y+3)^{2} & =2{(\\frac{x}{2}+5-2)}^{2} \\\\ 2{x}^{2}+(y+3)^{2} & =2{(\\frac{x}{2}+3)}^{2} \\\\ 2{x}^{2}+(y+3)^{2} & =2(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+3x+9) \\\\ 2{x}^{2}+(y+3)^{2} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+6x+18 \\\\ \\frac{3{x}^{2}}{2}-6x+(y+3)^{2} & =18 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}({x}^{2}-4x+4)-6+(y+3)^{2} & =18 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}{(x-2)}^{2}+(y+3)^{2} & =24 \\\\ \\frac{{(x-2)}^{2}}{16}+\\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{24} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the equation of an ellipse centered at $(2,-3)$ in the $xy$-plane.",
